**Given:**

Diagonals of rhombus, d₁ = 5 cm, d₂ = 12 cm

**Formula used:**

Perimeter of a rhombus = 4 × side

Side of a rhombus, s = sqrt{(dfrac{d₁}{2})² + (dfrac{d₂}{2})²}

**Calculation:**

s = sqrt{(dfrac{5}{2})² + (dfrac{12}{2})²}

⇒ s = sqrt{2.5² + 6²}

⇒ s = sqrt{6.25 + 36}

⇒ s = sqrt{42.25}

⇒ s ≈ 6.5 cm

Perimeter = 4 × 6.5

⇒ Perimeter = 26 cm

**∴ The correct answer is option 4.**
